s="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziyadat-allah-i">Ziyadat Allah I</a> crushes the rebellion in 827 with Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> help.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">827</span><span class="rf-text">Asad ibn al-Furat leads the Aghlabid conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, invited by the Byzantine rebel Euphemios.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">836</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziyadat-allah-i">Ziyadat Allah I</a> completely rebuilds the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-mosque-of-kairouan">Great Mosque of Kairouan</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">870</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabids</a> conquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">876</span><span class="rf-text">Ibrahim II moves his residence from al-Abbasiyya to the new palace-city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raqqada">Raqqada</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">902</span><span class="rf-text">Ibrahim II dies besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosenza">Cosenza</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-abdallah-al-shii">Abu Abdallah al-Shi'i</a> takes Mila, the first blow to Aghlabid rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">909</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutama-berbers">Kutama</a> rout the Aghlabid army near al-Aribus on 18 March; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziyadat-allah-iii">Ziyadat Allah III</a> flees to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and Abu Abdallah enters <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raqqada">Raqqada</a> on 25 March.</span></li></ol>
